  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes enough to serve 4 as a side and takes just 15 minutes to prepare, with 30 minutes resting time. It is a classic"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "asazuke"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", a quick-salted pickle you can make any night of the week."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Salt pulls water out of the vegetables and firms them up. Do not skip the resting step. Squeeze out as much liquid as you can before dressing them. This gives a crisper result and stops the dressing from going watery."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "cucumber",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": null,
              "prepNote": "halved lengthways and thinly sliced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "carrot",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "large",
              "prepNote": "peeled and cut into thin matchsticks",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sea-salt-fine",
              "amount": 1.5,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "rice-vinegar",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "caster-sugar",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sesame-oil",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sesame-seeds",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "toasted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put the cucumber and carrot in a bowl. Sprinkle over the salt and toss well. Leave for 30 minutes at room temperature."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tip the vegetables into a clean tea towel or a few layers of kitchen paper. Squeeze firmly to remove as much water as possible."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix together the"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "rice vinegar"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", sugar and sesame oil in a small bowl until the sugar dissolves."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the squeezed vegetables to the dressing and toss to coat. Taste and adjust if needed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Scatter over the sesame seeds. Serve straight away or chill for up to 24 hours. These are your"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tsukemono"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Pickles are too salty",
              "cause": "The salt was left on too long or not enough liquid was squeezed out.",
              "fix": "Rinse the vegetables briefly under cold water after squeezing and taste before dressing."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Vegetables are soft instead of crisp",
              "cause": "Liquid was not squeezed out properly before dressing.",
              "fix": "Squeeze more firmly next time. A quick 10-minute chill in the fridge after dressing also helps crisp them back up."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Dressing tastes too sharp",
              "cause": "The sugar did not dissolve fully, or the ratio of vinegar is too high.",
              "fix": "Add another half teaspoon of sugar and stir until dissolved. A tiny splash of water rounds out the sharpness."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tsukemono appear on tables across Japan at almost every meal. They range from months-long fermented daikon to quick fridge pickles like this one. This version uses the asazuke method, which is the quickest style of all. You find them served beside bowls of rice, on bento lunch trays, and next to grilled fish. They cut through rich flavours and refresh the palate."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}